# The build output, and only the build output. Everything under `src/` that is
# written by hand is source and stays tracked; everything below is written by
# `tools/build.mjs` (a board file compiled, an image turned into a list
# literal) or by the guest build, so it is regenerated rather than edited.
#
# Generated by `node tools/build.mjs` from the board file.
src/board/decode.rav
src/mem/sdram.rav
src/dev/flash_image.rav
src/rvboard/decode.rav
# Written one guest at a time, so it is never the same twice: `--guest linux`
# and `--guest doom` are two projects over one board.
src/rvboard/image.rav
# The RISC-V board's ALU tables and the Stage's size are generated too, from
# the same board file and the same `--stage` argument, so they are build output
# like the rest and are not committed.
src/rvcpu/tables.rav
src/cpu/luts.rav
src/screen.rav
src/rvscreen.rav

# The device trees `tools/build.mjs` renders beside the board file, and the
# flattened blobs it writes into `images/`.
boards/*.dts

# The guest images, built from source by `tools/wsl/`.
/images/

# The `.sb3`s, the pictures and the logs the checks write.
/dist/
